                <pb facs="0369" n="289" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg289"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hart to Mr.
                            Hay</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-11-30"><hi rendition="#italic">November 30,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hart, referring to the legation’s dispatch, No. 611, of May 15, 1902,
                    reports that the Colombian Government has ordered that all the Magdalena River
                    boats except three, which are not named, be returned to their owners.</p>
                <p>Mr. Hart understands that, until the indemnity is fixed, the boats of the
                    Cartagena company will not be received.)</p>
            </div>
